    <!-- ==== DEVICE TYPES ====================================================================
         DISPLAY LABELS ONLY. The stored value stays English in every locale - it is written to
         the override registry, matched by the Type column's color triggers, used as a CSS class
         in the exported report and accepted by the CLI's /type filter. DeviceTypeConverter maps
         one to the other on the way to the screen, and derives each key by stripping everything
         that is not a letter or digit ("Switch/AP" -> Str_Dev_SwitchAP).

         The list covers the classifier's whole vocabulary, not just the 21 rows in the "Set
         device type" menu: a type the menu cannot set can still be detected and shown.

         Product names (Windows, Linux, NAS, IoT, DNS, Apple, Android) are proper nouns and stay
         as they are when translated - only the surrounding words change. -->
    <sys:String x:Key="Str_Dev_Router">Roteador</sys:String>
